":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/194539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov","html_url":"https://github.com/mekhovov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mekhovov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":1915,"digest":"sha256:fb2bd96ee7ac3db962b69486e60e4cde84b67fb280450bfb47f5e7c99b20f33a","download_count":5,"created_at":"2026-09-23T05:20:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T05:20:00Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/releases/download/v0.91.0/verification.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mekhovov/revealline/tarball/v0.91.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mekhovov/revealline/zipball/v0.91.0","body":"## RevealLine v0.91.0 — Fair collision-only enemy movement\n\nOrdinary field enemies now hold a straight, readable course through open space and change direction only when they collide with a physical boundary or committed ground. New attempts use `gp4` / `field-course.v2`, with a small deterministic collision-only variation of at most eight degrees to avoid repeating axis and corner loops while preserving speed and the enemy's legal movement domain.\n\nThe new course rule does not sense the player, steer on a timer, cross domains, teleport, or alter special warning and committed attacks. Patrols, stationary keepers, capture rules, difficulty presets, administration controls, and bonus effects retain their existing behavior. Historical gp1, gp2, and gp3 saves and replays continue through their frozen adapters; existing attempts are not silently retuned.\n\nSource: `e771ca71b0e710ea878d54f8ff370707f7428ef8` (tree `9603f3df68b0b8bb8d370fdb9e83f39c9c508fe7`), merged through [PR #290](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/pull/290).\n\nThe exact-head [PR checks](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/actions/runs/35814330642) passed mandatory preflight and the production build. A focused source cohort passed 52 checks covering open-flight velocity invariance, horizontal, vertical, diagonal and corner collisions, one-cell corridors, speculative and partial commits, freeze/stun, equal seeded Versus and Team behavior, menu and administration continuity, completion eligibility, all compiled editions, and historical gp1/gp2/gp3 replay reconstruction. That cohort is separate from the waived full automated suites.\n\nThe actual merged-source [qualification and freeze](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/actions/runs/35820609785) passed source identity, validation, lint, formatting, native formatting, motion syntax, production reproduction/readiness, source-clean verification, and immutable freeze. Automated suites were explicitly waived under the temporary reviewed policy; no passing full-suite verdict is claimed.\n\nThe guarded read-only [artifact inspection](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/actions/runs/35821206253) verified every Git source blob/type/mode and source TAR commit, every distribution manifest byte and hash chain, and the bounded offline inventory. The PR-head-to-merge difference is limited to two accepted status/feedback documents and 51 accepted Pages-controller/preservation paths; no game, package, lockfile, workflow, or test content changed after the reviewed PR head.\n\nOriginal distribution: 591,145,167 bytes, SHA-256 `ff7615741415381e63cd386b9cd2cf777b8e5baa5e77c50f87b3e25bf4ed25f1`.\n\nOriginal source archive: 1,628,712,960 bytes, SHA-256 `fff248f44a69d998a809984680c1f0077360bfbd96e02738a824a0c7059f1cd1`.\n\nPages selection, v0.90 predecessor preservation, public byte verification, and bounded fresh-attempt browser checks remain separate acceptance gates until the selector PR is merged and the deployed site is checked. Whole-campaign balance, physical controllers, physical touch, cold-offline use, and musical/listening acceptance are not claimed by this release package.\n"}